## `select` (conc.select.2-6, ADR 1102): helpers for the passes that walk a
## statement's parts. A `select` evaluates its heads in source order (every
## arm's channel, a send arm's value and the `after` time), then waits, then
## runs at most one arm's block.

## The expressions a `select` evaluates before it waits, in source order.
pub fn select_heads(arms List[SelectArm]) List[Expr]
    mut out := List[Expr]()
    for a in arms
        match a.op
            Recv(_, _, ch) => out.push(ch)
            Send(ch, v) =>
                out.push(ch)
                out.push(v)
            After(ms) => out.push(ms)
            Closed => continue
    out

## The blocks of a `select`'s arms, in source order; at most one runs.
pub fn select_bodies(arms List[SelectArm]) List[List[Stmt]]
    [a.body for a in arms]

## The name a receive arm binds, or none.
pub fn select_var(op SelectOp) Binder?
    match op
        Recv(v, at, _) => Binder(name: v, pos: at, mutable: false)
        Send | After | Closed => none

## Whether a `select` always runs an arm: it has a `closed` or an `after`
## arm. Without one, a cancelled task's `select` that finds nothing ready
## runs no arm (conc.select.6).
pub fn select_always_runs(arms List[SelectArm]) bool
    for a in arms
        match a.op
            After | Closed => return true
            Recv | Send => continue
    false
